# Test fixtures must be BYTE-STABLE across platforms. Several checks here assert
# on exact bytes — a floors mutation locates a literal sentence, and the memory
# index parses a frontmatter fence — so a checkout that rewrites line endings
# changes the thing under test and the failure reads as a logic fault rather
# than a checkout one. Found by CI on its first Windows run.
#
# CRLF TOLERANCE IS A SEPARATE QUESTION AND IS NOT ANSWERED HERE. This governs
# THIS repo's own files. Handling a CRLF file supplied by a USER is the tool's
# job, and is covered by a unit test rather than by a checkout setting.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The deleted-tests log is an unordered set of one-line rows that every change
# deleting a test file appends to, so two such changes touch the same place. A
# union merge keeps both sides' rows; the class test reads the rows as a set
# (a repeated row is one row), so a line in either order or twice is the same
# declaration. Only this ledger has that shape: the counted allowlists carry a
# `# ceiling:` line and rows an update removes, which a union merge would
# resurrect or duplicate.
internal/ci/testdata/deleted-tests.txt merge=union

# The append-only records: a header, then one row per key (the first field), rows only
# appended, so two changes that each add a row at the end touch the same place. A union
# merge keeps both sides' rows; the lander then drops a row held twice and refuses a key
# held by two different rows (cmd/nova-sprint/landrecords.go; docs/STANDARD.md section
# 10, the file classes). A hand resolution of these once deleted seven measured rows.
tla/CASES.tsv merge=union
tla/RUNS.tsv merge=union
